From: Jakub Jirutka <jakub@jirutka.cz>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 20:07:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Skip test_gettimeofday on 32-bit platforms

The test declares struct timeval with two long fields, which is 8 bytes
on 32-bit platforms. However, musl uses 64-bit time_t on 32-bit
platforms (time64), so struct timeval is 16 bytes there. gettimeofday()
then overflows the allocated buffer, which corrupts the heap and crashes
Ruby with SIGSEGV when the struct is freed.

--- a/test/fiddle/test_import.rb
+++ b/test/fiddle/test_import.rb
@@ -460,6 +460,10 @@
     end
 
     def test_gettimeofday()
+      if SIZEOF_VOIDP < 8
+        omit("Timeval is declared with long, but time_t is 64-bit on 32-bit platforms (musl, time64)")
+      end
+
       if( defined?(LIBC.gettimeofday) )
         LIBC::Timeval.malloc(Fiddle::RUBY_FREE) do |timeval|
           LIBC::Timezone.malloc(Fiddle::RUBY_FREE) do |timezone|
